From e0af98f46ec125e089b4c4b8e24f76adc4be62f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:10:20 +0000
Subject: ipa: soft: Keep the black level exact, by gain, and its noise

Three things lift the shadows off black, and the AWB gains then tint
what is lifted, blue under warm light (blue gain ~2.2 against red
~1.05), and the tone curve brings it up:

- The black level is held as an 8-bit integer, the 16-bit value
  shifted down: a 10-bit pedestal of 63 (4032) is taken as 15, not
  15.75, leaving 0.75 above black in every pixel. Hold it as a float.
- Sensors' black level can drift with analogue gain; the S5KJNS
  module's vendor tuning has it fall from 4032 at 1x to 3664 from
  64x. Accept a blackLevelGain piecewise linear function of the gain
  and apply each frame's level by the gain it was taken with, in the
  debayer and, for its statistics, to AWB and AGC.
- The debayer clamps each channel at 0 after the AWB gains, so the
  noise around black, half of it below, averages to a positive
  offset in dark areas. Keep values below black through colour
  correction and clamp only before the tone curve.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
